# Modernize Legacy Barva‑Bladet Issue Agent

## Goal
Improve readability of old Barva‑Bladet HTML issues with **minimum changes** that are
repeatable across many files:

- Add a modern `<head>` baseline (viewport + Bootstrap + `site.css`)
- Place a consistent top backlink aligned with content width
- Wrap the legacy content in a centered, readable container
- Use **scoped CSS** (`body.bb-legacy`) so modern pages are unaffected

This agent is for legacy issues under `assets/barva-news/<year>/...`.

---

## What “minimum changes” means (hard constraints)

- Do **not** rewrite, reflow, or re-author the newsletter content.
- Do **not** delete legacy tables/`<font>`/Word markup; just make it readable.
- Do **not** change `src` / `href` paths (except adding the backlink wrapper).
- Do **not** move files or update the archive listing page.
- Keep diffs mechanical and repeatable.

---

## Target structure (what to end up with)

### 1) `<html>` and `<head>`

Ensure the document starts with:
- `<!doctype html>`
- `<html lang="sv">`
- `<meta charset="UTF-8">`
- `<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">`
- Bootstrap 5 CSS include
- `site.css` include

For issues under `assets/barva-news/<year>/...` the CSS path should be:
`../../../assets/css/site.css`

Keep any tiny in-file legacy style blocks only if needed (don’t expand them).

### 2) `<body>`

Set the body to:
- `class="bb-legacy"`
- Keep legacy `bgcolor` attribute if present (don’t fight it)

### 3) Backlink placement (top bar)

Immediately inside `<body>`, add:

```html
<div class="container-lg bb-topbar">
  <a href="../../../index.html" class="back-link">
    ← Tillbaka till Barvabygden.se
  </a>
</div>
```

### 4) Main content wrapper

Wrap the existing legacy content (everything after the backlink, before the footer bits)
in:

```html
<main class="container-lg bb-issue my-3">
  ...existing legacy content...
</main>
```

Do not restructure inside this wrapper.

---

## CSS requirement (shared, scoped)

Confirm `assets/css/site.css` contains the “Legacy Barva‑Bladet issues (readability helpers)”
block with rules that are scoped to `body.bb-legacy`, including:

- `.bb-issue` background + padding
- `body.bb-legacy p, body.bb-legacy .MsoNormal` line-height + spacing + `text-align: left !important`
- `body.bb-legacy img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; }`
- `body.bb-legacy table` mobile overflow handling
- `body.bb-legacy .bb-topbar` spacing
- `body.bb-legacy .back-link` pill/button styling + focus state

If the block is missing, add it at the end of `site.css` (scoped only to `bb-legacy`).

---

## Workflow

1) Read the target issue HTML file.
2) Apply the mechanical HTML edits above:
   - modernize `<head>` (only the baseline)
   - set `body.bb-legacy`
   - insert `.bb-topbar` backlink wrapper
   - wrap all content in `<main class="container-lg bb-issue my-3"> ... </main>`
3) Verify `site.css` contains the scoped legacy helpers; add if missing.
4) Quick sanity checks:
   - page still has exactly one `<html>`, one `<head>`, one `<body>`
   - backlink path stays `../../../index.html`
   - images still resolve (no path edits)

---

## Output required

- File processed
- Whether CSS legacy helper block was already present or added
- A short list of the exact mechanical edits performed (no commentary)

